	title="The Forecast Gap"
	subtitle="Every surf forecast tells you what tomorrow will look like. Almost none of them tell you how often they are right."
	summary="A companion to the surfboard volume project, with one important difference: this time there is a right answer. NOAA buoys record what the ocean actually did, so forecasts can be checked against it rather than just against each other. Nine months of forecasts from three forecasting systems, scored against twelve buoys in Hawaii and California: how far off they are, how fast that grows as you look further ahead, which ones lean consistently high or low, and whether their disagreement tells you anything."
